test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T11:52:51.4311082Z             "body": "This private fork preserves the original stdio MCP surface and adds bounded local batches and durable jobs. Production readiness remains incomplete; this PR stays draft.\n\nThe current candidate fixes the reproduced VP9 matrix-tag color shift by deterministically preparing pinned Playwright/core1.64.1 with `-colorspace smpte170m` at build time and bundling that runtime pair. Exact input/output hashes fail closed on unknown bytes. There is no runtime interception or recorded-file rewriting. A scripts-disabled production install verifies that both entry points resolve the same prepared core. Caller-supplied contexts/remote Playwright servers retain their host encoder. See docs/DEPENDENCY_PATCHES.md for provenance, upgrade review and payload tradeoffs.\n\nAdditional changes retain bounded journal initialization phases on failure, advertise existing workflow scalar limits, and add nested-shadow/virtual-list tests. Media tests preserve strict pixel thresholds and the original5s visible readiness wait, add a source-paint witness and bounded failure state diagnostics. Windows independent legacy checks can run after a completed original-suite failure; no failed case is retried, deadline raised, default transport changed or historical ownership evidence cleared.\n\nValidation on the combined source: PCM/video4/4 each Node20/22/24 (Chromium/Firefox); source-painted color controls8/8 (baseline4/8); production297-file tarball installed with scripts disabled and all original/batch/jobs/journal/guardian smokes passed; actual Codex0.163 app-server1,000 actions/37.4s, zero model turns and zero owned processes. Strict typecheck, generated-doc lint, actionlint and14 build/reporter guards pass. Local Docker build stopped at npm certificate validation; no TLS/trust bypass was attempted. Native image hash and browser validation remain required. WebKit engine tests were not executed locally.\n\nLatest completed native84 at096b617 failed: batch1287/2, original486/8. Windows main batch never ran after installed guardian `journal_open/init rpc_timeout`; Mac raw/SDK and actual Codex880 timed out; media includes gray/shifted frames and Windows WebKit readiness failures. Four separate Mac1k pipe/server controls passed without proving a causal fix. All17 completed-job logs and the initial failed EOF read are archived. Older missing birth ledgers,136/142 process cohorts, cleanup uncertainty and other acceptance gaps remain open. No merge or publication is proposed.\n\nNative85 verifies23b07fd:\n- [Local batch QA39768881695](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39768881695)\n- [Original CI39768881668](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39768881668)\n\nEvidence and gate status: docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_REPORT.md, docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_LEDGER.md, docs/evidence/native84-followup-archive.json and docs/evidence/native85-combined-proof.json. Pending CI outcomes are not passes.\n",
